# Secrets KNOWN to be in this repository's git history.
#
# This file is not an allowlist of things that are fine. It is a register of
# exposures that have already happened and cannot be undone by deleting a
# file: the blob stays in the pack until the history is rewritten, and anyone
# who cloned before that has it regardless. Every line is an OUTSTANDING
# OPERATOR ACTION, reprinted on every run until the entry is removed.
#
# It exists because a gate that is permanently red is a gate people switch
# off, and the point of the scan is to catch the NEXT one.
#
# Format:  <sha256-prefix>  <what it is>  |  <required action>
# The digest, never the value — recording the secret here would put it in the
# tree as well as the history.

2ca1d13600a428db  BIP84 zpub, committed in CLAUDE.md 2026-08-18 (f09db4cd), present in 8 revisions until removed  |  CONFIRM PROVENANCE. It is NOT the wallet pinned in scripts/wallet.pin and NOT the BIP84 spec test vector, but it is a structurally valid key that derives real bc1q addresses. If it was ever generated from a seed the operator controls, MOVE THE FUNDS: an extended public key cannot be rotated, and whoever has it can watch that wallet's whole balance and payment history forever.

37dc8c2ee9531e53  BIP84 zpub, committed in btcpay/runbook.md 2026-08-18 (f09db4cd) in a copy-pasteable command  |  CONFIRM PROVENANCE, same test and same remedy as above. This is the "real example key in a copy-pasteable runbook command" CLAUDE.md records being caught once already — caught in the tree, never in the history it was already in.
